---
// Figure 1 of the kagent showcase (headquarters, branch kagent-paper, refarch-kagent.html), ported:
// Turf and kagent 1.0 in one cluster. Left, kagent's namespace: the UI where a person approves, the
// controller, and the Agent "turf". Middle, Agent Substrate: the agent's gVisor sandbox, which holds
// no credential, and the egress gateway that adds the bearer token to every call. Right, everything
// Turf: the MCP server, restate-server and the engine as a Knative RestateDeployment that scales from
// zero, with the state as Secrets and Leases. Geometry is the paper's; fills and strokes are the
// `.f-*`/`.s-*` utilities. Markers come from FigureDefs. Rendered once per page.
---

<svg class="fig kagent" viewBox="0 0 672 318" role="img" aria-label="Turf and kagent 1.0 in one cluster. kagent: the UI, the controller, and the Agent turf with its Harness, AgentTemplate, ModelConfig and RemoteMCPServers. Agent Substrate: the agent's gVisor sandbox on the WorkerPool in the kagent namespace, and the egress gateway in ate-system. turf: the MCP server, restate-server as a RestateCluster, and the engine as a RestateDeployment on Knative, from zero pods, with the state Secrets and Leases. Arrows: the person approves in the UI; the sandbox calls the MCP server through the gateway, which adds the bearer token; the server drives restate-server; restate-server calls the engine through Knative; the engine applies to the cluster.">
  <text x="0" y="10" class="t-cap">TURF AND KAGENT 1.0, ONE CLUSTER</text>

